tgs:Human.JosephTainter a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Joseph Tainter"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Joseph Tainter (human)"@en ;
    owl:sameAs <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Joseph_Tainter> ;
    rdfs:comment "Archaeologist and anthropologist; Professor, Environment and Society Department, Utah State University since 2007 (Department Head, 2007-2009). Author of the real 1988 book The Collapse of Complex Societies, developing a real, technical distinction between complexity (structure plus organization) and mere complication (structure without organization) as the basis for a cost-benefit theory of societal collapse. Co-author, with Tadeusz Patzek, of Drilling Down: The Gulf Oil Debacle and Our Energy Dilemma. Real, direct personal significance to Nate Hagens: Nate's own words describe reading Tainter's work, alongside Herman Daly's, as directly causing him to leave his Wall Street career."@en ;
    .

