tgs:Human.KateRaworth a thinkr:Human, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kate Raworth"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Kate Raworth (human)"@en ;
    thinkr:memberOf tgs:SchoolOfThought.DoughnutEconomics ;
    owl:sameAs <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kate_Raworth> ;
    rdfs:comment "English economist (b. Dec 13, 1970); creator of Doughnut Economics (first developed in her 2012 paper 'A Safe and Just Space for Humanity,' elaborated in her 2017 book), co-founder of Doughnut Economics Action Lab. Senior Associate, Oxford University's Environmental Change Institute; Professor of Practice, Amsterdam University of Applied Sciences. Member, Club of Rome; serves on the WHO Council on the Economics of Health for All."@en ;
    .

tgs:Human.NateHagens a thinkr:Human, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nate Hagens"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Nate Hagens (human)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The graph's primary subject — this individual was notably absent until 2026-07-11 despite the entire graph being organized around his framework. NO owl:sameAs: verified 2026-07-11 he has no genuine Wikipedia page (the only hits are EverybodyWiki, not real Wikipedia, and an unrelated Wikidata entry Q51905132 for a different person entirely, 'Nathan A Hagen,' an ORCID-linked researcher with no connection to energy/TGS — confirmed via search, not assumed). Credentials (per the publications/credentials CV scope, not full employment history): PhD in Natural Resources, University of Vermont; Master's in Finance with Honors, University of Chicago Booth School of Business. Pre-TGS career: VP at Salomon Brothers and Lehman Brothers, President of Sanctuary Asset Management, before leaving Wall Street circa 2002-2004. Real, direct cause confirmed in his own words during TGS_27 (Joseph Tainter): reading Tainter's 'The Collapse of Complex Societies,' alongside Herman Daly's work, directly caused him to leave Wall Street — 'a life changing recognition.' Not modeled as a formal thinkr:influencedBy triple (that property is deliberately scoped to Concept/SchoolOfThought-as-subject only, not Persona-as-subject — see its own declaration in tgs-core.ttl for the reasoning); kept here as biographical prose instead. TEACHING, genuine tense conflict between sources as of 2026-07-11 — his own site (natehagens.com/about2) says PAST tense, 'For eight years, Nate taught Reality 101, an honors course at the University of Minnesota'; other sources (RateMyProfessors, Resilience.org) use PRESENT tense. Not resolved either way, flagged honestly rather than guessed. 'Professor' title itself is informal/student usage (RateMyProfessors) — his own bio consistently says 'taught'/'teaches,' never asserts the formal rank. tgs:Work.RealityBlind was the course's primary text (confirmed via a LinkedIn post from Nate himself)."@en ;
    foaf:givenName "Nathan"@en ;
    foaf:familyName "Hagens"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Commonly known as 'Nate' (see skos:prefLabel) — 'Nathan' confirmed as his fuller given name via his own X handle, @NJHagens = Nathan John Hagens. Deliberately not resolving which form foaf:givenName 'should' hold here — flagging the real ambiguity rather than silently picking one, same as the deferred firstName/lastName backlog item. foaf:homepage MOVED to tgs:Persona.NateHagens 2026-07-15 (see that individual's own scopeNote) — a homepage is a public-facing fact like every other Relationship/Episode/Concept-influence fact already migrated under design decision 0f, not biography. It deliberately does NOT include thegreatsimplification.com or its YouTube channel — those arguably belong to TGS THE SHOW as its own entity (not currently modeled at all, same real gap as ISEOF/his employer, also unmodeled despite being confirmed real) rather than to Nate personally. Flagged, not resolved."@en ;
    dbo:birthDate "1969"^^xsd:gYear ;
    thinkr:memberOf
        tgs:Organization.TheOilDrum, 
        tgs:Organization.PostCarbonInstitute, 
        tgs:SchoolOfThought.PeakOilMovement, 
        tgs:AcademicInstitution.UniversityOfVermont, 
        tgs:AcademicInstitution.UniversityOfChicago, 
        tgs:AcademicInstitution.UniversityOfMinnesota .

