    rdfs:comment "Spanish physicist and scientist (b. 1970, León); PhD in Theoretical Physics, Autonomous University of Madrid. Senior scientist, Institute of Marine Sciences, CSIC (Barcelona), specializing in satellite oceanography, turbulence, and sea surface salinity/temperature/currents. Better known publicly as editor of the real, influential Spanish-language blog 'The Oil Crash' (El Otro Cronista/Crash Oil), an early and prominent voice on peak oil and resource depletion; author of 'Petrocalipsis' (2020) and an advocate for degrowth. Real prior TGS solo appearance confirmed: Episode #65 ('Deep Challenges: Oceans, Scarcity and Culture')."@en ;
