tgs:Human.FrancisWeller a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Francis Weller"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Francis Weller (human)"@en ;
    owl:sameAs <https://www.francisweller.net/> ;
    rdfs:comment "American psychotherapist (MFT, retired), writer, and self-described soul activist; 40+ years developing what he calls soul-centered psychotherapy, synthesizing psychology, anthropology, mythology, alchemy, indigenous cultures, and poetic traditions. Founder and director, WisdomBridge (educational programs integrating indigenous and Western wisdom traditions). Author of the bestselling 'The Wild Edge of Sorrow: Rituals of Renewal and the Sacred Work of Grief' (real, direct originator of the 'Five Gates of Grief' framework), 'The Threshold Between Loss and Revelation' (with Rashani Réa), 'In the Absence of the Ordinary: Soul Work for Times of Uncertainty,' and 'Entering the Healing Ground' (the official Wild Edge of Sorrow workbook). Real endorsement from Joanna Macy (already discussed extensively in this graph's own RR-17 build) appears on his own book jacket. BA, University of Wisconsin-Green Bay; two Master's degrees, John F. Kennedy University."@en ;
    .

