tgs:Human.BillPlotkin a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bill Plotkin"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Bill Plotkin (human)"@en ;
    owl:sameAs <https://www.animas.org/about-us/our-founder/> ;
    rdfs:comment "American eco-depth psychologist, wilderness guide, and self-described agent of cultural evolution; founder, Animas Valley Institute (southwest Colorado, 1980/1981), guiding thousands of people through nature-based initiatory passages, including a contemporary Western adaptation of the pan-cultural vision fast. PhD, psychology, University of Colorado Boulder; earlier career as a research psychologist (studying nonordinary states of consciousness), university psychology professor, psychotherapist, rock musician, and whitewater river guide. Real, direct origin story for his current work: in 1979, during a solo winter ascent of an Adirondack peak, he experienced what he calls a 'call to spiritual adventure' that led him to leave academia. Author of 'Soulcraft: Crossing into the Mysteries of Nature and Psyche,' 'Nature and the Human Soul: Cultivating Wholeness and Community in a Fragmented World,' 'Wild Mind: A Field Guide to the Human Psyche,' and 'The Journey of Soul Initiation: A Field Guide for Visionaries, Evolutionaries, and Revolutionaries.'"@en ;
    .

#############################################
# ADDED 2026-08-13 — TGS_213 bootstrap. Independently verified via
